diffs.patch:
Index: openwiki/.claims/change-guides.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/change-guides.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/change-guides.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,150 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:015d439d4ebf47f49a608f88108ae990607011cb3605af33fbfc99419050c7d6",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f5421917f40e4644992e413105dc7b29",
+      "statement": "Environment parsing is strict: an unset variable selects its caller's documented default, while a supplied variable must contain a valid value, so a typo cannot silently change the configuration of a running node.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/env_vars.rs#L3-L7",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2aa04b70a8a9dba1576b358daf010acc27ecad86843eea1c5767460cb19d0ade:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_fd11a615f42846a3b9d313f7e0f11ed1",
+      "statement": "The env_vars::validate pass validates every typed production variable before the runtime starts, because some consumers cache a value or read it from a synchronous callback and cannot return a configuration error at the point of use.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/env_vars.rs#L16-L99",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6a6f8e4cbddb98b3c7bd61e0e2030a28d32031736946a56fa733dfabfcc9c339:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3a59a8facb804d71aaca866b4f87e9ec",
+      "statement": "celld deploy accepts an allowlist of Wrangler config keys (SUPPORTED_KEYS); anything else is an error, because refusing is compat-safe while guessing produces confusing activation failures later.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/deploy.rs#L36-L56",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19d196eeeab34d583e9da587fced8e7570209026a0237093e4e3b74f74eacd73:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_904dcfcf7e7c471ca96e8441d873730d",
+      "statement": "Each deployable feature (assets, cron, D1, KV, queues, R2, sqlite-vec, wasm, workflows) is gated by a FEATURE_*_V1 constant in SUPPORTED_DEPLOYMENT_FEATURES so a node that cannot load the feature refuses the manifest at deploy time rather than failing on first use.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/protocol.rs#L54-L99",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:80c90de9306aeffe34a4740ac6071b65736b3b457d4f02403a154caa23ec0a9f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c12a789153b549deba1827a4dae41426",
+      "statement": "Worker binding types (services, variables, R2, D1, KV, queues, workflows, assets, and the loader) are carried as lists in the WorkerConfig shape in crates/celld/js.rs.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js.rs#L1747-L1778",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e9b25611525a0999cb2afb983bc76cea41d3575572dbb03d99e368836cf0b0d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_02c079c5d26846b285fbf7b7245375d4",
+      "statement": "The R2 binding surface is implemented in the JS harness as globalThis.__makeR2Bucket, served out of the fleet bucket under the binding's key space.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js/harness.js#L1001-L1001",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:405bbed3d1c967f258c42c3fe651fbb24b0b80b9f85c5f9e8e25ba191f8b31a3:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_cd5e3b0c0aaa4b54a4d50a3669952658",
+      "statement": "KV bounds ship as data (__cell.kvLimits) that the JS harness compares against, because reaching Rust from the harness costs a host op and a second Rust implementation would be a copy nothing called.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/kv.rs#L9-L17",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4874eb8207dc298fc6c2a5b85cf016460fd4be24f529db9a3ee510fe1b63f2a9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4e0e7c5e0bf64ead851b1cbc9ad32bfd",
+      "statement": "The coordination protocol vocabulary is changed by adding inputs to the Event enum and outputs to the Effect enum in crates/logic/types.rs, which are the only way in and the only way out of the core.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L401-L402",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b480b5378674b2b8a1ea00fab27a07f4491d69302f1f0059a8336f6d1590d324:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8a046db9ba3c462fb005d7568beeec44",
+      "statement": "Every asynchronous effect is versioned, and completion events with an obsolete op are ignored, so new effects must follow that contract or late completions corrupt state.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L737-L744",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:192519c856f93735a48d940303ae874ff5b632cc9bd8a894415446b5e3523fa9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2bdbe3c9d9b44d7c85831467067d7a63",
+      "statement": "The ownership effect adapter deliberately contains only serialization, wall-clock sampling, SDK configuration, and error classification; ownership decisions remain in celld-logic.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L3-L7",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53089c7c3cf4f752f149b5550e97163c9d6cb889702d8adc68d3c98c676644eb:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a818d47c7e1f40e691d81fdf908766e7",
+      "statement": "put_cas answers Ok(None) only for a clean 412/409 rejection; every other failure is ambiguous because the write may have committed.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L20-L24",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:87a60adc0e4f479dd4365a62475a2c87612ec70a014849fa56ebd9b221395daa:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_153ea25ca0ac43e289f1b9b1c2b05e8e",
+      "statement": "The TLA+ specifications are a hand-synced snapshot deliberately not in continuous integration, and their updates land in the same changes that moved the protocol.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L73-L79",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f44fb427214c9f1c6f3b3cc997fcc91752eac696baa2234bc2b23f90abcbaa7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_333a38a323194e81bbfd125ec0b12b58",
+      "statement": "Compatibility flags are honored through the Compat struct built from manifest metadata by worker_compat, which applies the enable/disable flag and the compatibility_date switch.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L483-L522",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3c367993fb8c0653f13ab6dfe873544512478f6fd231c142e6b5d6e3f6e379d8:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_809464b80fed428398c97da52b5c3bfc",
+      "statement": "The celld_internal_tests cfg switches in the simulated asyncrt and the conformance suites, so deterministic invariants surface in-crate before a live-fleet run.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L300-L320",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cee2fbcbf3747b9dffbc96637713a27fc8c13d3407ab786dfbbae3c97227fb8d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T15:05:17.667Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/deployments.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/deployments.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/deployments.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,170 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:8abd0bc88420e07b3a9ae9e3ac92b5dc957267c6ce79deb91f79796112e877ef",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f86a31d290e8471490cf8073b2d095ab",
+      "statement": "celld deploy does config, identity, and durable bucket publication: bundling is esbuild's job, and the module never shells out to wrangler or speaks a Cloudflare-shaped API.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/deploy.rs#L8-L13",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01d76c11fbae99ded394c034b5f42f2c60fee0da993fd809502c09a68c76d1c0:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9edb2009d9494e9c9b5c048d83202861",
+      "statement": "The durable deployment objects in the bucket are the interface between deployment tools and celld; nothing else is exchanged.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/protocol.rs#L3-L5",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb5044783b76d4672530c51e5b467c22b00142d6221fbfdf4401e80d716be9d2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_928c584f6a964cad92fb30c401101b9a",
+      "statement": "The deploy manifest (deploy/<script>/<version>/manifest.json) carries schema version, script name, main module, Durable Object classes, SQLite-backed classes, module refs, assets, crons, queue consumers, required features, and the raw Wrangler metadata.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/protocol.rs#L11-L44",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0ee52dff5da06de9b19517c2003cea40e71f611cc304ec7ae98518c182535392:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ecde313732cb476b8472a9d281580f77",
+      "statement": "deploy/current.json is the fleet-wide pointer a node reads on startup; changing it is a deploy and nodes converge to it, and it carries a rollout percent.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/protocol.rs#L401-L417",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:453e9797178f6f6931bf3e1c2ce7489716c7a155f37cf3d3d410d4550842d576:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_59306d6088e1401f9b0059b403ef6547",
+      "statement": "The asset index (deploy/<script>/<version>/assets.json) maps paths to immutable asset entries with SHA-256, byte size, and content type.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/protocol.rs#L333-L339",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c1cf03929bccf7b3a3b8cfd935a53bee11a6be9314ce8219ba3010fea6f49a7f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9336c4675afe41708cc80a0561f1b8b2",
+      "statement": "Asset bodies are content-addressed under deploy-blobs/assets/sha256/<aa>/<hash>, keyed by a validated SHA-256 digest.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/protocol.rs#L393-L398",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f9f88f69186dbd01fb036f681ba2902e52b34cca42ec0d9ca160a08ff325e502:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_58340b6c56c94aab9b40c2613d6f239a",
+      "statement": "A deployment version is the deterministic hash of the sorted module contents, the serialized metadata, and the asset index; cron expressions are deliberately not an input because a schedule is configuration layered on top.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/protocol.rs#L420-L435",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6b437108345a09f78025d1f2a71d6f02da3f3cd860e39b9bec9bf2b61a11be0a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_bbbbfa0752cb470b8482c8c3f8aa1195",
+      "statement": "celld deploy accepts an allowlist of Wrangler top-level keys (SUPPORTED_KEYS) and refuses anything else; the compatibility doc adds that it accepts wrangler.jsonc or wrangler.json and never wrangler.toml.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/deploy.rs#L36-L56",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19d196eeeab34d583e9da587fced8e7570209026a0237093e4e3b74f74eacd73:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b4ff02a233bc409985090eb0c8fc53e8",
+      "statement": "Each deployable surface is gated by a FEATURE_*_V1 constant, and a manifest requiring a feature this build cannot load is rejected up front so the failure moves from request time to deploy time.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/protocol.rs#L50-L99",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cd54135c20dc64ec1895b974c1d3828bd18b23e6a25fb7e5dc1808693d529940:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_59f546b611c248c7a3af8f43834e119e",
+      "statement": "The runtime supplies four reserved Durable Object classes, __D1Database, __Workflow, __KvNamespace, and __Queue, and a user config naming a reserved class in durable_objects or migrations is refused.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/deploy.rs#L58-L81",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a2bb80fe05999e636025fe978f49938ec7a1f6d1cf93c44a5d4eccebd4bde937:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_eeca16e04d28478892b06abd504ed146",
+      "statement": "The asset resolver can adopt a newer foreign asset index through a fallback source, because during a rolling restart content-hashed asset paths can point at an index a not-yet-restarted node has never heard of.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/assets.rs#L35-L47",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:339b42ce9513bdd4aed11621779145aca5e75d35237518bd7e77ee35f034f248:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c678e9d61a4e409d88c24c9ac7944851",
+      "statement": "A generation is everything a node derives from a deployment — compiled Worker configurations, isolate pools, the Durable Object class registry, service bindings, asset resolvers, and cron schedule — and a request that started on one generation finishes on it even after the node adopts another.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/generation.rs#L3-L16",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:62fdfda1f2ae66dcc76f4e1193dc0b968821a1ead6e2502c376aba169e3c567c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5da977b0b32e45afaebb3aabd15b4bea",
+      "statement": "Boot and reload construct a generation through the same two functions (DeploymentGraph::load and Generation::build), so a reload cannot miss what a boot did.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/generation.rs#L12-L16",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a21c75b405ec3cfb6b9d50f420d65aded49a54958c5231721e21db8b82a1804:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_eede7cc6a3f5496d9e4e26f57bb1e6fb",
+      "statement": "Each node reads deploy/current.json every CELLD_DEPLOY_POLL_S seconds (default 30) and adopts a new deployment in place; POST /reload adopts it now, a node builds the new deployment beside the current one and switches new requests in one step, and a deployment that does not build leaves the current one serving.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L245-L253",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8ee191ea2b8465c36fe7011a68a8cd60c01c24f4333506d943b8bea7d0c0fe7b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_041f3f643bcf4d47a8d5fb121fa744e7",
+      "statement": "A resident Durable Object moves to a new deployment at a safe point (no request, alarm handler, durability wait, or regular WebSocket), is forced after CELLD_DEPLOY_MAX_AGE_S seconds (default 60, 0 forces at once), and in the adoption window a request on one deployment can call a Durable Object on the other.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L258-L271",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aa92aefd7aa365ce7996634a09504e51f359bcf09ac1d8ef1a0c5d86dc8fcdd1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ac2cb7d0223747238d54d31dfb128777",
+      "statement": "Durable deployment objects are validated before they become runtime state; validate_queue_manifest re-runs the authoritative celld-logic checks when a node loads either a native or a managed manifest.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/protocol.rs#L168-L205",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e78f21d5f1db8696e698bed4f4740c2677742b9852c701bcfad63a18955d0ccd:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T15:05:17.667Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/memory-and-pressure.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/memory-and-pressure.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/memory-and-pressure.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,170 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:b30f3e1dea749f62af4f82ed6d191cb74f1423ed3c7ff0f5a01a0a100baa3368",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ea714b5b448b4f668f96fe07ab0a1144",
+      "statement": "Resident-cell count is a hard cap enforced at admission, while the pressure classifier answers only whether the node is out of memory and must give cells back; conflating the two produced placement churn and an admission wedge.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L3-L14",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0dd600768a3c2d7976136d9049625b51436ee370a877bd530077dec64a929bad:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_019d005a70a0408a9244883369fefc46",
+      "statement": "A memory sample obtains four measurements in one sampling turn: process RSS, in_use_bytes (RSS minus allocator slack), the cgroup working set (memory.current less inactive_file), and the complete cgroup current charge.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/memory.rs#L22-L31",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:65223537a1c530547412cb7ab88cd5908afeb9579f5b07195525f2c188a9a861:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7995c11fa245457ab509e1db78a3f216",
+      "statement": "in_use_bytes is RSS minus the pages jemalloc keeps but nothing uses, computed from stats.resident less stats.allocated after advancing the allocator epoch.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/memory.rs#L164-L178",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1bf3a3c0239a48af838cec2ccf071d30145faab234262bddd9ec7d5b3ae19485:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_26fddefd3229487099e4b3290f9b6e6b",
+      "statement": "On a readable Linux memory cgroup, the working set is memory.current less the inactive_file charge from memory.stat, which includes active kernel charges that process RSS does not report and excludes file and allocator pages.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/memory.rs#L39-L99",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f563a080f3bfcfaee85360eca34e18bd33f1d1a5b9b3a7183b6669dd1ec365b1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4c5abe65a4b448a8af76575fd71eb4e4",
+      "statement": "celld enables jemalloc's background thread at startup so freed pages return even when a node that just shed its working set does not allocate again; on macOS the thread is unavailable so the absolute cap is the only protection against an OS kill.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/memory.rs#L188-L196",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b142c4702a5490ac78b2b3de4edf13840362d551f358fb7bba12f2ffce04c11:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5e7bf124a9314821b10988cde8a3b75e",
+      "statement": "PressureConfig is built from the environment: high_bytes defaults to 80% of the available memory and CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB=0 disables it, while rss_hard_bytes is an absolute cap of 95% of the available memory on the complete cgroup charge, never derived from the ceiling.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L151-L177",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b22ec479a08a5f9a6f61d897002840ad772843dd967e2b7bcac8cc868a861305:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4b899607e5004093944418da94395a51",
+      "statement": "When the machine size is unknown, the absolute cap falls back to 125% of an explicit ceiling, which is worse than a share of the machine and better than no floor at all.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L148-L150",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aad8f7da287543a0197843112f0ac9d7a598285c5a949fd598344eccc91ef4f2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_259f78082f504d5dac03c09289820f81",
+      "statement": "Pressure shedding uses two independent latches, memory and rss_hard, so one crossing can never hold the node against the other's watermark.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L46-L58",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6b11663b2a1c7fe385e20d505ba88c0916ae31284dc03091140fa4874a999fd7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_da318166c3de4212b92205bebfd2d639",
+      "statement": "Each ceiling engages at its own ceiling and releases at its own low watermark of 80% of that ceiling; the classify function reports the reason with the hard cap first because it is the more serious.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L192-L230",
