+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f98e513a3f304e2a97b52b9d6d22ea5e",
+      "statement": "The walk down works against Metric::InUse whenever the ordinary ceiling is latched because eviction relieves it, and the shedding target is about one tenth of the measured resident cells per pass.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L248-L277",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bcc82a52cc08bf2b8b4bf19f548ca3eb29dd27240533eb56ec9c5f33050a9145:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d73300a9d92f4f76b7e5ea1ad5697647",
+      "statement": "Config::max_evictions bounds how many evictions may hold a durability proof in flight at once, because a proof is a round trip to the bucket and the bound is what makes a shed walk down finish in a bounded time.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L74-L80",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cdeef2a89cdb37694aa67b1feeacd9c45eac9cb3285bdea9576b660a7c5a8727:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8498a015e13f42ff9491079c25447915",
+      "statement": "Config::max_resident is a hard cap on resident cells plus activation reservations, enforced at admission.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L63-L67",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:423fd2be7a0310cc3a9431aa5c12aac237d902faa4676714fb372ed990357668:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f4501c8dae9f46239f0a262cd627b457",
+      "statement": "has_headroom is a stricter state than not pressured: a node can be below the high watermark without enough room to absorb a donor, and a rollout uses this state.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L232-L242",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:70fa285e5d8eb17d772a78906512c545746f9feab18b325801693db6a1822fee:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_407b08ff810a46a2b3efb25afac4f21c",
+      "statement": "Each isolate has a separate V8 heap limit, default 128 MB matching a Cloudflare Durable Object; an isolate above 90% refuses a new hibernatable WebSocket, an isolate at the limit stops materializing a SQL result set, and it serves again when heap use falls under 75% of the limit.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L297-L311",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a1c9ea044d529a2baafcecf5ecccf0075022aba71c120758c9c45547f925cb46:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3c0a979159c4411793135ef6e1dafb6e",
+      "statement": "At most 50% of the resident cap may be pinned by outbound WebSockets, counted in pinned cells rather than sockets and never rounded below one.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L279-L296",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f20602e58cf3c8c2293edde91cd8c402f77a2a2621b477c9a41b4cecc34c0f2f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c74cd7b5699b4784bda1b9fda903a197",
+      "statement": "Under pressure celld durably replicates and fences the least-recently-used idle cells, publishes them as unowned without resetting their epochs, refuses to reacquire new unowned cells, and does not shed a cell with active work or a live host WebSocket.",
+      "evidence": [
