+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4bb3e98211484dcca3608a9668b17f5c",
+      "statement": "Telemetry is off by default and the off state is structural: init never runs, start_trace finds no globals and answers None, and no event is ever built.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L6-L12",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:03ec58ec5a1168d8cde3fe3edad1d6350088821664df6453ed9be482f8842bd5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_407529d7a7804d9ca30990ea50694128",
+      "statement": "The default sink is the fleet bucket, writing Parquet under the telemetry/ prefix with no other service; the alternative sink sends the same data to an OpenTelemetry collector, and the schema is version v0-unstable carried in each file's object metadata.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L7-L15",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3c194b6dd15e47812e0e6a0f3bc5124724cd06d8aa6bb1b569ab2c6b4503ed0c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0244db6e2f7842ca98e6b9647e5dac7d",
+      "statement": "Telemetry config is built once by Config::from_env, which returns None unless CELLD_OTEL is set to 1.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L102-L108",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:737f41ab3dfa9ed52df2368fd4d1921e0cc43b6d76a854868124980c16af5730:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2075fb298f7744de87dfe018c1472409",
+      "statement": "The telemetry settings — CELLD_OTEL_SINK, CELLD_OTEL_BUCKET, CELLD_OTEL_RETENTION (default 30d), CELLD_OTEL_FLUSH_MS (default 300000), CELLD_OTEL_FLUSH_BYTES (default 5242880), OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, and OTEL_SERVICE_NAME — are parsed by Config::from_lookup.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L110-L209",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:397789b913c36891db33d4ab63bb8c71b962d5fddb75d089aceafaa8ec3216fb:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_75654b450cd44db9b899e759b6f164de",
+      "statement": "The bucket sink flushes when the time limit or the size limit is reached first, keeping a busy node's Parquet objects near the flush size instead of thousands of slivers per hour.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L92-L97",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:affb1de1143129e15dcd3f935fdfbcfc080e2c52de28f427a2f91797dcdb37a1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8b04a3c49a7846bf83c5c5e31ef0991b",
+      "statement": "The sampler defaults to parentbased_always_on, and traceidratio/parentbased_traceidratio require OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG in [0, 1]; a parentbased sampler defers to the caller's sampled flag and decides only for roots.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L140-L162",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3eb7ea46a5c19112acec4d38d3697a9d0f82bd2ae418075329cc818fca782eb6:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4dccadc1192c479892faac60d86a7b1c",
+      "statement": "celld records a span for each stateless Worker request, each cell event, each outbound fetch, and each cell start; records each console.log line with the trace id and span id of the handler so logs join traces across awaits; and reads and sends the W3C traceparent header to join the surrounding traces.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L35-L50",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a2ef719d398485d5dc63965b3d55230e3fd4a9d8982d53d37d8e4f51f69dee1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5cd720969cf64ec5b7aac8a4be2f403f",
+      "statement": "The telemetry hot path never blocks: record is a try_send, a full channel increments a drop counter, and under saturation telemetry sheds counted rather than shedding requests.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L14-L19",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1ce47b0c21e6bf2d931542407575120c8dbc8f00a63058debb7c1d80c971b28e:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a71cbd09d8d74b7e8d8127e9ed05d7f0",
+      "statement": "A console.log body larger than 8 KiB is truncated because log records are telemetry, not blob storage.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L35-L39",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:879b9d6e7b1885baa78d8c0ba70b0be55daa9ea21fa9a86074f7323332474acf:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_682434bbeb7f4914bbbb29cfd7b20cc9",
+      "statement": "celld records no metrics yet; the spans carry durations and queue waits, so many questions a metric answers have an answer in the traces.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L56-L59",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e2e2d57f3cf831553117160941fddec134c147ee0caeab6e9add03d88332dbdf:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_add02f69023e4858a4c1a8d4898befca",
+      "statement": "Telemetry files are partitioned by node and by hour under telemetry/traces/<node>/<yyyy>/<mm>/<dd>/<hh>/ and telemetry/logs/..., so a query that reads one day touches only that day's files.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L87-L89",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:962ab3d8430cab10740a6ed54521c76ed35495f69d8cc34d47adb33345e25b34:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9ada826ea0ff45a7bc024c88b2a74f09",
+      "statement": "celld does not compact its own telemetry files; a compaction job must run on a maintenance node once an hour for the hour that just ended, rewriting one past hour of small files into one large zstd-compressed file with DuckDB.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L112-L134",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b0e44941f12e40a93fa9e63eb8402a4e183b4fdfcade9f08a11084ec1ca23d8:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3fb3c4165b644615878188a0993d8b1d",
+      "statement": "The OTLP sink hand-encodes OTLP/HTTP protobuf so prost, tonic, and the generated proto crates stay out of the binary, the same trade the Parquet sink made by skipping arrow.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/otlp.rs#L3-L11",
